#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Legacy: pre-CLI installs' bin/harness-upgrade replaces itself with this file; it points them at the harness CLI.
cat >&2 <<'MSG'
The harness is now a CLI. Install it once, then run `harness install` from this repo to remove the old bin/ scripts:

  curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Eschults/harness/v1/install.sh | sh

From then on: harness upgrade, harness doctor, harness issue <number>, harness uninstall.
MSG
exit 1
